.TH OMX-PANEL-SYNC 1 "2026-11-24" "omx-panel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-panel-sync \- the one sync pass: descriptions stored, then port groups and MOD GUIs from the store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-panel-sync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omx-panel-sync
runs the omx-panel sync in one pass. First
.B omx-panel sync
gives each LV2 plugin on LV2_PATH its entry in the descriptions store, once: read when a layer holds it, else derived
and written to the layer of the effective uid (the system layer as root, the user layer otherwise); then that layer
loses the entries of plugins no longer installed (another binary, or a URI no bundle declares). No other layer is
written. Then
.BR omx-complement-sync (1)
and
.BR omx-modgui-sync (1)
run as they run alone, reading the store the first step filled.
.PP
It never runs systemctl: run by hand it does the whole work, and the unit is a batch convenience over it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
LV2_PATH, MODGUI_DIR, STATE_DIR and DESCRIPTOR_DIRS, as
.BR omx-complement-sync (1)
reads them; LV2_PATH unset is MODGUI_DIR first, then /usr/lib64/lv2:/usr/lib/lv2:/usr/local/lib/lv2.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/omx/modgui-sync.conf
KEY=value lines for the variables above, read by the unit
.TP
.I omx-panel-sync.service
runs the pass once; enabled by default where systemd exists (80-omx-panel.preset; the DEB enables it), it runs at boot
and each time plugin-qualify-sync finishes (a drop-in, plugin-qualify-sync.service.d/omx-panel-sync.conf, queues it
from ExecStartPost when the unit is enabled). Nothing depends on it: systemctl disable omx-panel-sync turns it off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every step finished
.TP
.B 1
a step did not; each one is named on standard error
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx-complement-sync (1),
.BR omx-modgui-sync (1),
.BR omx-panel (1),
.BR omx-panel-store (1)
